# Resume App Code Rules

## Imports and Exports
- Use named exports for components: `export function Component()` or `export const Component = ()`
- Import from aliases: Use `@/components/*` instead of relative paths
- Group imports: React/Next.js first, then third-party, then internal imports
- Sort imports alphabetically within each group

## File Structure
- One component per file unless components are tightly coupled
- Filenames should be kebab-case.tsx for components, kebab-case.ts for utilities
- Page components go in app/*/page.tsx
- Reusable UI components go in components/ui/
- Layout components go in components/
- Utilities go in lib/
- Group server actions by feature in app/actions/ directory

## TypeScript
- Always define proper types for props using interfaces
- Name interfaces with suffix: ComponentProps, e.g., `interface ButtonProps`
- Avoid any types whenever possible
- Use React.ReactNode for children props

## Component Style
- Use functional components with arrow syntax for smaller components
- Use function declaration for larger, more complex components
- Always use explicit return types for functions that return JSX: `function Component(): JSX.Element`
- Use React.forwardRef for components that need ref forwarding

## CSS and Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Use the cn() utility from @/lib/utils for conditional class names
- Follow the shadcn/ui pattern for component variants using cva()
- Use CSS variables for theming in conjunction with next-themes

## MDX Content
- Use custom components from MDXProvider for consistent styling
- Properly handle code blocks with syntax highlighting
- Error handling for MDX parsing should be user-friendly

## State Management
- Use React hooks for local state
- Prefer useReducer for complex state
- Keep state as close to where it's used as possible

## Server Actions (Next.js 15)
- Separate data logic from presentation
- Centralize API calls in server actions
- Organize actions by feature in dedicated directories
- Return data, not JSX from server actions
- Add proper error handling with clear error messages

## Performance
- Use client components only when necessary
- Use React 19 features like useFormStatus and useOptimistic when appropriate
- Memoize expensive calculations with useMemo
- Optimize re-renders with useCallback for event handlers
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Consider using the experimental React Compiler for automatic memoization

## Accessibility
- Ensure proper keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper heading hierarchy
- Support both light and dark themes
- Use shadcn/ui components which have built-in accessibility features

## Code Quality
- Follow ESLint rules defined in eslint.config.mjs
- Keep component files under 250 lines
- Write clear, self-documenting code
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Use the "after" API for code that needs to run after response streaming
